# Smart Irrigation System using Arduino

A complete automated irrigation system that monitors soil moisture and controls watering based on real-time sensor data. This project uses Arduino microcontroller to manage an efficient, water-saving irrigation solution for gardens, farms, and indoor plants.


## 🎯 Project Overview

The Smart Irrigation System automates the watering process by monitoring soil moisture levels. When moisture drops below a threshold, the system automatically activates a water pump. This ensures optimal watering, prevents overwatering, and reduces water wastage while keeping your plants healthy.

## ✨ Features

- **Automatic Watering**: Triggers pump when soil moisture is too low
- **Real-time Monitoring**: Continuous soil moisture level tracking
- **Manual Override**: Option to manually control the pump
- **LED Status Indicators**: Visual feedback for system status
- **Adjustable Thresholds**: Customize moisture levels for different plant types
- **Low Power Operation**: Efficient power management
- **Multiple Zones Support**: Can be extended for multiple irrigation zones

## 🛠️ Components Required

### Hardware

| Component | Quantity | Specifications |
|-----------|----------|-----------------|
| Arduino Microcontroller | 1 | Arduino Uno, Mega, or Nano |
| Soil Moisture Sensor | 1-N | Capacitive or resistive type |
| Water Pump | 1-N | 5V/12V DC submersible pump |
| Relay Module | 1-N | 1-channel or multi-channel relay |
| Power Supply | 1 | 5V/12V DC adapter |
| Jumper Wires | As needed | Male-to-male, Male-to-female |
| Breadboard | 1 | Standard 830-point breadboard |
| LED Indicators | 2-3 | 5mm Red/Green LEDs |
| Resistors | 2-3 | 220Ω for LEDs |
| Push Button | 1 | For manual control (optional) |
| Water Pipe/Tubing | As needed | 6-12mm diameter |

### Software

- Arduino IDE (version 1.8.0 or higher)
- USB Cable (for programming Arduino)

